sequenceDiagram
    participant CM as CronManager (sibling pod)
    participant Gate as eFTI Gate (admin endpoint)
    participant DB as PostgreSQL
    participant Log as ECS JSON log

    Note over CM: Daily — operator-set<br/>time (default 03:45).<br/>YAML schedule in<br/>cronmanager-expire.yaml.<br/>HTTP POST job → admin<br/>expire endpoint.

    CM->>+Gate: POST /api/v1/admin/expire-identifiers<br/>Authorization: Bearer ${BEARER_OPS_TOKEN}
    Gate->>Gate: Auth: literal compare with ARCHIVE_OPS_TOKEN env var
    Gate->>Gate: Acquire concurrency guard via advisory lock — 409 ARCHIVE_IN_PROGRESS if already held

    Gate->>+DB: Resolve the latest row per dataset_id where mode='road',<br/>status='active', and transport_date + 14 days has passed.
    Note over DB: Cabotage retention —<br/>Reg 2024/1942 Art 11(4).<br/>Latest-row resolution<br/>per db/README.md.
    DB-->>-Gate: candidate dataset_ids (e.g. 550e8400-…, a1b2c3d4-…, c3d4e5f6-…)

    loop For each expired road consignment
        Gate->>+DB: Append a new consignments row sharing the same dataset_id<br/>with status='inactive' (denormalised columns copied from the prior latest row).
        DB-->>-Gate: written
        Note over DB: Append-only — no UPDATE.<br/>New row is the latest.<br/>DISTINCT ON dataset_id<br/>now reads 'inactive'.
        Gate->>Log: { event.action: "identifier.expire",<br/>efti.dataset.id: "550e8400-…",<br/>efti.expiry.reason: "cabotage_14d" }
    end

    Gate->>+DB: Append a jobs_execution_log row (job_name='expire-identifiers',<br/>status='completed', details: { expired_count: 3 })
    DB-->>-Gate: ok
    Gate->>Gate: Release concurrency guard
    Gate-->>-CM: 200 OK { expired_count: 3, duration_ms: 14210, dry_run: false }

    Note over CM: Non-road modes are NOT<br/>expired — cabotage rule<br/>applies to road only<br/>(Reg 2024/1942 Art 11(4)).<br/>Old rows archived nightly<br/>by CronManager (Epic 26).
